# ʻEwa DP dashboard

News Room site: `index.html`, served by `server.py` for internal team use.

Structured news lives in `data/news.json`. Project records may also live in `data/projects.js` as `window.EWA_DP_DATA`.

No logins. An internal **Upload** form is allowed so people with the team link can add a PDF, Word, or text file as a new Needs review entry. Do not add a public-facing CMS, accounts, or City/DPP branding.

## Ingest (mandatory)

When the user drops files in `ewa-dp-inbox/`, attaches a source, pastes a URL, or asks to import / ingest / add / tag material:

1. Read the source. Do not invent facts. If a date, place, agency, or completion is not in the source, leave it blank or "Not identified".
2. Match an existing project when it is the same effort under a different name. Create a new project only when it is truly separate.
3. Propose project tags (reuse existing tags when they fit).
4. **Stop. Show the proposed tags and ask the user to confirm, remove, add, or revise them. Do not write `data/projects.js` or `data/news.json` until they confirm.** Exception: files posted through the internal Upload form may be saved immediately as Needs review stubs.
5. After confirmation, add a dated update and a separate source under the project. Use new stable IDs (`proj-`, `upd-`, `src-`, `st-`, `ms-`, `geom-`).
6. If status, decision, schedule, funding, scope, location, or responsible party changed, append status history and milestones. Never overwrite old chapters.
7. Update current status from the newest reliable source. Keep conflicts visible.
8. Add map geometry only when the source supports it. Mark uncertain locations `approximate`.
9. Set `needsReview: true` and `status: "Needs review"` on new/changed records. Set `sourceType` to Link, PDF, Word, or Text.
10. Skip ingest if a card already has the same `sourceUrl` or `sourceFile`.
11. Tell the user to refresh the HTML board, review Needs review cards, and say what to fix.

A reversal, delay, redesign, funding change, approval, denial, or party change is a new history chapter on the same project — not a silent replace and not a duplicate project.

